alwaysApply: true
---

User Interaction (via MCP Tools)
	•	Always use the designated MCP tools (ask_user_buttons, ask_user_text, ask_user_confirm) for any interaction, input, or confirmation steps in this project.
	•	Before implementing any task or code change, and AFTER proposing a plan, you must:
	•	Break down the plan into clear subsections (e.g., 1.2.1.3…) for reference.
	•	Use server.tool("ask_user_confirm", ...) to obtain explicit approval from the user.
	•	Do not mark any task as completed without:
	•	Using server.tool("ask_user_confirm", ...) to get confirmation from the user that it was completed correctly.
	•	Before summarizing or closing a task:
	•	Use server.tool("ask_user_confirm", ...) to verify the summary with the user.
	•	For major design decisions (e.g., changes to public interfaces or architecture refactors):
	•	Use server.tool("ask_user_text", ...) or ask_user_buttons to gather input from the user and follow their direction.
	•	Avoid unnecessary prompts:
	•	Only use MCP tools to engage the user when their input is needed for important decisions or confirmations.
